# Pinned Aether toolchain versions for CI — the single place to bump.
#
# aeb tags are "later means later" markers, NOT semver promises; pin them so a
# CI run is reproducible. `ci/toolchain.sh` reads these; override at the shell to
# test a bump (e.g. `AETHER_REF=v0.591.0 ci/run.sh`).

# The Aether compiler (`ae`). Tag vX.Y.Z, branch, or commit SHA.
# Pinned to 0.643.0. The floor remains 0.638.0 — it carries the WebSocket client
# the BiDi work needs (std.http.ws_connect, first in 0.590 — see
# docs/WebDriver-BiDi.md) AND the single-file-module fix (aether aeec9b69 +
# a34ec231, "Accept single-file modules in [package] modules") that this repo's
# aether.toml [package] modules line depends on: `ae add
# github.com/aether-lang-dev/selaenium@<tag>` + `import webdriver` resolves with
# NO --lib only on >=0.638.0 (on 0.637.0 it was wrongly rejected as "does not
# exist"). 0.640-0.650 build the engine and all bindings clean, including the
# 6-platform cross-compiled jar matrix (verified on ae 0.650; aeb v0.300 pins
# 0.650 for its own build, and the ecosystem tracks it).
AETHER_REF=v0.650.0

# The aeb build runner. Tag v0.NNN, branch, or commit SHA.
# v0.303 made the Ruby SDK tool-named (breaking): ruby.install/minitest/rspec/
# rubocop → ruby.bundle(){ install() minitest() ... }, and ruby.package(){ gemspec }
# → ruby.gem(){ build(...) } (the gem_dir edge is unchanged, so ruby/.example.ae
# is untouched). selaenium's ruby/.tests.ae + ruby/.package.ae were migrated to
# the new verbs. v0.305 added: ruby.bundle hard-errors on a bare block-setter
# call (safety; our nodes already use the block form), and an rbenv grammar.
# v0.306 finalized the rbenv declaration as a bare flag `rbenv()` (+ optional
# ruby_version("3.3.1")) — NOT `ruby_env`/`ruby_manager` (both had issues: the
# `env` setter mangles to `ruby_env` so a `ruby_env` function segfaulted; fixed
# upstream in aeb, and the rbenv routing now resolves via the rbenv SHIM so
# bundle install/exec share the gem home). selaenium's ruby/.tests.ae declares
# rbenv() (this box runs an rbenv-managed Ruby 3.3.12; the system apt Ruby 3.1 is
# too old — bundler can't swap the default cgi gem). v0.307 adds cpp dep-object
# linking (cpp.tests links a C dependency's pre-compiled objects) — REQUIRED by
# the C++ client (cpp/), which links the C client's selenium.c compiled AS C so
# its extern "C" symbols aren't C++-mangled. Also additive: java.package_jar
# from_classes() (opt-in) and --graph run-colouring. v0.300
# (carried forward) standardized the arch word on
# x86_64 (assets aeb-<os>-x86_64.tar.gz + -musl variants; bldr._host_os_arch()
# emits <os>-x86_64); selaenium tracks that in ci/toolchain.sh, the crossbuild
# lib names + jar /native/<os>-<arch>/ paths, and Native.osArch() (still accepting
# the JVM's amd64 as input). Also folded in: size() (v0.296), copy-only bundle
# installer (v0.298), bldr._host_arch/_host_os_arch.
AEB_REF=v0.307
